{
  "id": "veridical-perception",
  "term": "veridical perception",
  "definition": "Veridical perception is the claimed accurate acquisition of information in a way that appears to occur without ordinary sensory input, such as reports during out-of-body experiences of perceiving from a location outside the body. In this context, it refers to information that can be independently confirmed as correct.",
